{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"chauvinist-subsolar-arctichare","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Steering an auto-resumed completion verification away from already-searched places (negative frontier, advisory not hard-exclusion to avoid permanent blind spots) and toward where credited evidence was found (positive frontier) requires per-call argument-level transcript telemetry (paths read, search queries run) that the verifier workflow does not currently capture. Two-part capability: (1) transcript capture in the LLM runner telemetry; (2) deterministic frontier-digest extractor + resumption prompt injection, scoped within a single close invocation (same pinned ref), never persisted cross-run. Parent: adolescent-evilminded-locust implements unsteered auto-resume (proven sufficient live via 8d74 re-close 2026-08-14); this idea upgrades it if unsteered resumption proves insufficient at scale.","id":"19ea-29af-ebb3-410b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"status":"idea","tags":[],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Search-frontier handoff for completion-verifier resumptions (needs argument-level tool-call transcript)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786766946660572001,"uuid":"349273b5-b709-47c2-a364-9fce72b1420d"}